  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Initialize thicknesses from iteration_11 best candidate: [92.0, 45.0, 99.0, 120.0, 69.0, 120.0, 51.0, 120.0, 119.0, 46.0, 120.0, 45.0, 120.0, 47.0, 120.0, 60.0, 120.0, 84.0, 120.0, 65.0, 120.0, 75.0, 46.0, 70.0] nm. Identify the 8 layers with largest thickness values (indices: 3,5,7,10,12,14,16,18 all at 120.0 nm, then select next largest). Constrain optimization to perturb only these 8 layers; fix remaining 16 layers at initial values. Use gradient_thickness optimizer with learning rate scaled to 0.05x of default. Apply conservative acceptance: reject any step reducing best_target_score below 0.7524 (iteration_11 historical best) by more than 3%. Evaluate at normal incidence, unpolarized, coherent TMM. Spectral bands: 200-400 nm (maximize reflectance), 800-1500 nm (maximize transmittance). Thickness tolerance: ±15 nm absolute normal deviation for robustness. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 200-400 nm, 800-1500 nm. soft objectives: High transmission in 800-1500 nm band; High reflection in 200-400 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Low transmission in 200-400 nm band; Low reflection in 800-1500 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layers <= 30; Materials limited to HfO2 and SiO2.",
